# DGang deployment (Oracle free tier, nynmondal host)

## Stack
- Node backend: Express + Socket.IO on `:3000` (systemd `dgang.service`)
- Frontend PWA served by same Node (or nginx proxy)
- nginx reverse proxy: `dgang.bad.mn` → `127.0.0.1:3000`
- HTTPS: Let's Encrypt via certbot
- Media: uploaded to `/home/ubuntu/social-app/media/`

## Files
| File | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `dgang.service` | systemd unit (`/etc/systemd/system/dgang.service`) |
| `nginx-dgang.conf` | nginx vhost → `/etc/nginx/sites-{available,enabled}/dgang.bad.mn` |
| `finalize.sh` | run after DNS is live: verifies DNS, issues cert, reloads nginx |

## First-time deploy
1. **DNS** (afraid.org / FreeDNS): add `A` record
   `dgang.bad.mn -> 140.245.252.78` (server public EIP). Wait ~5 min.
2. Install systemd:
   ```bash
   sudo cp deploy/dgang.service /etc/systemd/system/
   sudo systemctl daemon-reload && sudo systemctl enable --now dgang
   ```
   NOTE: `ExecStart` uses `/home/ubuntu/.local/bin/node` (v26). The ancient
   `/usr/bin/node` (v12) can't parse `body-parser` — never use it.
3. Install nginx vhost:
   ```bash
   sudo cp deploy/nginx-dgang.conf /etc/nginx/sites-available/dgang.bad.mn
   sudo ln -sf /etc/nginx/sites-available/dgang.bad.mn /etc/nginx/sites-enabled/
   sudo nginx -t && sudo systemctl reload nginx
   ```
4. Once DNS resolves, finalize SSL:
   ```bash
   ./deploy/finalize.sh
   ```
5. Verify: `curl https://dgang.bad.mn/api/health`

## Common ops
- Restart: `sudo systemctl restart dgang`
- Logs: `sudo journalctl -u dgang -f`
- Socket.IO + nginx: the `/socket.io/` location forwards Upgrade headers — required.
- Caching: html/js/css are never cached (network-first) so bug-fixes reach users fast.

## Ports
- `:3000` — Node backend (localhost only, no direct firewall exposure)
- `:80` / `:443` — nginx internet-facing